# Build output — regenerated by `quarto render`, never committed.
_site/
.quarto/
/.luarc.json
*_files/

# Screenshots and measurements taken while verifying a layout change. Scratch
# output of a render, same as _site/ — regenerate it rather than commit it.
_verify/

# NOTE: _freeze/ is deliberately NOT ignored. It is the committed execution
# cache that keeps published posts reproducible.
# See CLAUDE.md § The three rules that matter, rule 1.

# R
.Rproj.user/
.Rhistory
.RData

# Python
__pycache__/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# Local-only, deliberately untracked. This repo is PUBLIC.
# ENVIRONMENTS.md maps this machine — software inventory and versions, MCP
# server wiring, where API keys are kept, open unfixed issues. Useful to agents
# working here, a reconnaissance document to anyone else. Keep it on disk; keep
# it out of git.
#
# CLAUDE.local.md is the cross-session handover — dropped subjects, half-written
# posts, names not yet public. Claude Code loads it alongside CLAUDE.md, so it
# works exactly like the committed guidance without becoming permanent public
# history. Durable rules belong in CLAUDE.md or .claude/rules/ instead.
#
# .claude/rules/*.md IS committed — it is shared guidance. Only the local
# permission grants below are per-machine.
ENVIRONMENTS.md
CLAUDE.local.md
New Text Document.txt
.claude/settings.local.json

# OS / editor cruft
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store

# Quarto's jupyter-engine intermediates. Ours, and the one that actually works:
# an interrupted render leaves index.quarto_ipynb_1, _2, … and only the trailing
# star catches those.
**/*.quarto_ipynb*

# ── Below this line is maintained by Quarto, not by hand. ────────────────────
# `quarto publish` rewrites this file and re-appends these two exact patterns
# whenever they are absent. Both are already covered above — `.quarto/` at the
# top of this file, and the starred pattern immediately above — so they are
# pure duplicates. Deleting them only makes them reappear on the next publish.
# Leave them.
/.quarto/
**/*.quarto_ipynb
